# Local PCG Extension Notes

This document records the local changes made for the user's Unreal TA workflow.

## Goal

Keep `chongdashu/unreal-mcp` updateable from upstream while adding project-useful PCG and Unreal Python automation.

The extension avoids adding a separate C++ command for every TA operation. Instead:

- C++ adds one generic `execute_python` command.
- Python MCP tools call that command.
- PCG-specific behavior lives in Python and can evolve quickly.
- Crash-prone editor APIs get focused native commands. In particular, PCG attribute/property selector structs must use `set_pcg_attribute_selector` instead of Unreal Python selector mutation.

## Current Branch Model

- Cubeless integration/default branch: `main`
- Legacy extension branch: `local/pcg-tools`
- Base upstream at time of extension: `4e5f00d`
- Initial extension commit: `ecab023`

## Current Bridge Port

- This UE 5.6.1 fork uses UnrealMCP editor bridge port `127.0.0.1:55561` by default.
- Keep `55561` separate from the older UE 5.7 bridge port `55557` so both editor lines can be used on the same workstation.
- Override only when needed with `UNREAL_MCP_5_6_1_PORT` or the editor command-line option `-UnrealMCPPort=`. The generic `UNREAL_MCP_PORT` is intentionally ignored by this fork so existing UE 5.7 sessions can keep using it.

## Files Added

- `AGENTS.md`
  - Instructions for Codex/AI agents. Read first.
- `Python/tools/python_tools.py`
  - Registers `execute_unreal_python`.
- `Python/tools/pcg_tools.py`
  - Registers PCG-focused automation tools. Fast PCG refresh and spline point sync use native UnrealMCP bridge commands first, with Unreal Python fallback for older running editor sessions. PCG selector struct mutation is native-only and has no Python fallback.
- `Python/tools/controlrig_authoring_tools.py`
  - Registers recipe-driven ControlRig authoring adapter tools that call the
    editor-only `UUnrealMCPControlRigAuthoringSubsystem` from the
    `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor` module through Unreal Python reflection
    instead of adding a static UnrealMCP C++ dependency.
- `Python/tools/editor_tools.py`
  - Adds native viewport bookmark listing, bookmark/active viewport screenshot wrappers for visual QA, and protected editor level transition preflight/opening.
- `Python/tools/ai_tools.py`
  - Adds AI authoring support inspection, stable BT/BB helper wrappers, saved BT/BB inspection, a saved Behavior Tree execution smoke, and a temporary SIE patrol/detection/chase smoke for the default Cubeless character path.
  - Uses `create_ai_patrol_chase_behavior_assets` for standard Unreal Behavior Tree/Blackboard authoring through the editor-only C++ bridge.
- `Python/tools/texture_generation.py`
  - Registers Codex built-in handoff texture tools, heuristic companion-map generation, texture-set import, PBR material creation, and optional material application helpers.
- `Python/services/openai_image_service.py`
  - Keeps a disabled compatibility shim for legacy API-key image generation imports; this project does not use API-key image generation.
- `Python/services/unreal_texture_importer.py`
  - Wraps Unreal Python UV export, texture import, PBR material/material-instance creation, and material application helpers.
- `Docs/Tools/pcg_tools.md`
  - User-facing tool summary.
- `Docs/Tools/ai_texture_tools.md`
  - User-facing AI texture tool summary.
- `scripts/update_with_pcg_extension.ps1`
  - Helper script for updating from upstream and keeping the local branch.

## Files Modified

- `Python/unreal_mcp_server.py`
  - Imports and registers `python_tools`, `pcg_tools`, and
    `controlrig_authoring_tools`.
- `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/UnrealMCP.uplugin`
  - Enables `PythonScriptPlugin`.
- `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/UnrealMCP.Build.cs`
  - Adds `PythonScriptPlugin` dependency.
- `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/Public/Commands/UnrealMCPProjectCommands.h`
  - Declares `HandleExecutePython`.
- `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/Private/Commands/UnrealMCPProjectCommands.cpp`
  - Implements `execute_python` using `IPythonScriptPlugin::ExecPythonCommandEx`.
- `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/Private/UnrealMCPBridge.cpp`
  - Routes `execute_python` to project commands.
  - Stops accepting commands as soon as engine exit or subsystem deinitialization begins, and rechecks queued game-thread/ticker work before dispatch.
  - Tracks subsystem lifetime separately from TCP listener readiness, so an occupied bridge port does not disable the in-process command registry or hide the startup failure status.
- `MCPGameProject/Source/MCPGameProject.Target.cs`
  - Set to UE 5.6 compatible build settings/include order.
- `MCPGameProject/Source/MCPGameProjectEditor.Target.cs`
  - Set to UE 5.6 compatible build settings/include order.
- `mcp.json`
  - Historical sample MCP launcher config. Active Cubeless projects using this repo should use a relative sibling path such as `../UnrealMCP5_6_1/Python`.

## Added MCP Tools

- `execute_unreal_python(code, mode="ExecuteFile", defer_to_ticker=false, allow_unsafe_editor_scripting_during_pie=false, interchange_policy="auto")`
  - Unsafe editor actor cleanup calls such as `EditorLevelLibrary.destroy_actor` are blocked during PIE/SIE by default.
  - Python map transitions and Python PCG attribute selector struct mutation are blocked by default because both have caused editor crash paths.
  - Source-code strings are not used to classify imports. `interchange_policy="auto"` conservatively behaves as `legacy`, moves the script to the next editor tick, and temporarily routes synchronous `AssetImportTask`/`import_asset_tasks` or `AutomatedAssetImportData`/`import_assets_automated` calls through legacy factories. Use `none` only for a script that cannot import; this is a trusted declaration, not a sandbox. Use `preserve` (or `interchange`) for synchronous direct `UInterchangeManager.import_asset`, `reimport_asset`, or `import_scene` calls and formats that require Interchange. A scripted async Interchange call must wait for completion and read back its result before Python returns; an import still active at return is reported as an unknown in-flight mutation. Import-capable policies are rejected inside synchronous `batch` execution. Python asset Force Delete and Python-driven editor shutdown remain focused accident guards rather than a security sandbox.
  - Legacy live smoke scripts that embed Python Force Delete cleanup are intentionally rejected until their cleanup is migrated offline or to a reviewed native route; they are not stability checks for this guard.
- `set_blueprint_node_positions(blueprint_name, graph_name, updates, dry_run=true, compile=false, save=false)`
  - Guarded layout-only batch edit for existing Blueprint nodes. Validates every GUID, class, exact title, and expected position before changing only `NodePosX`/`NodePosY`; rejects duplicate GUIDs and PIE/SIE, with a 2048-update maximum.
  - Requested real compile/save failures return `success=false`; a compile failure skips saving and reports that positions may already have changed.
- `collapse_blueprint_nodes_to_function(blueprint_name, graph_name, function_name, node_ids, dry_run=true, compile=true, save_asset=false)`
  - Guarded editor-only extraction through Unreal Engine's native Blueprint `Collapse to Function` implementation. It blocks PIE/SIE, duplicate or stale GUIDs, existing function names, and non-temp assets unless `allow_non_temp=true` is explicit.
  - The authored Blueprint function and call node are ordinary engine content; the command does not serialize UnrealMCP classes or runtime dependencies into the asset.
- `list_pcg_assets(root_path="/Game")`
- `list_pcg_components()`
- `refresh_pcg_components(actor_name="", selected_only=false, cleanup=true, generate=true, wait_until_complete=false, timeout_seconds=10.0, poll_interval_seconds=0.05, max_components=1000)`
- `inspect_pcg_component_outputs(actor_label="", actor_name="", actor_path="", actor_tag="", actor_label_prefix="", component_name="", component_tag="", selected_only=false, max_components=16, max_tagged_data=64, max_points=8, include_point_samples=true)`
  - Native read-only `FPCGDataCollection` readback for generated component output, including sampled `UPCGBasePointData` transforms, density, bounds, color, seed, and metadata entry values.
- `set_spline_component_points(points, actor_label="", actor_tag="", actor_label_prefix="", component_name="Road_SourceSpline", closed_loop=false)`
- `set_pcg_attribute_selector(graph_path, node_id, selector_property_name, selector_type="attribute", attribute_name="", selected_property_name="", domain_name="", point_property="", extra_property="", extra_names=None, reset_extra_names=true, save=true, dry_run=false)`
